{
  "agent": {
    "commands": [
      "kubectl -n astronomy-shop get pods -o wide 2>&1; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp 2>&1 | tail -40",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get deploy 2>&1; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout history deploy/ad 2>&1; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout history deploy/flagd 2>&1; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get deploy ad -o yaml 2>&1 | head -150",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get deploy flagd -o yaml 2>&1 | head -200; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' 2>&1; echo; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop logs deploy/flagd -c flagd --tail=30 2>&1; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop logs deploy/ad --tail=30 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop top pods 2>&1; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get pods -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,CPU_REQ:.spec.containers[*].resources.requests.cpu,CPU_LIM:.spec.containers[*].resources.limits.cpu 2>&1 | head -40; echo ---; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap user-config -o yaml 2>&1 | head -30",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o json | python3 -I -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); f=json.loads(d[\"data\"][\"demo.flagd.json\"]); f[\"flags\"][\"adHighCpu\"][\"defaultVariant\"]=\"off\"; d[\"data\"][\"demo.flagd.json\"]=json.dumps(f,indent=2); print(json.dumps(d))' > /tmp/flagd-config-fixed.json && kubectl -n astronomy-shop apply -f /tmp/flagd-config-fixed.json 2>&1 && kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' | grep -A6 '\"adHighCpu\"'",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' | grep -c '\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"'; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' | grep -B8 '\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"' | head -12",
      "cd /tmp; CUR=$(kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}'); NEW=$(printf '%s' \"$CUR\" | sed 's/\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"/\"defaultVariant\": \"off\"/'); kubectl -n astronomy-shop create configmap flagd-config --from-file=demo.flagd.json=<(printf '%s\\n' \"$NEW\") --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl -n astronomy-shop apply -f - 2>&1; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' | grep -A9 '\"adHighCpu\"'",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout restart deploy/flagd 2>&1 && kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout status deploy/flagd --timeout=180s 2>&1; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout restart deploy/ad 2>&1 && kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout status deploy/ad --timeout=180s 2>&1; sleep 60; kubectl -n astronomy-shop top pods 2>&1 | grep -E 'ad-|flagd-'; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get pods 2>&1 | grep -vE ' 1/1 +Running| 2/2 +Running| 4/4 +Running'; echo \"non-ready pods above (none = all healthy)\"",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop exec deploy/flagd -c flagd -- cat /etc/flagd/demo.flagd.json 2>&1 | grep -A8 '\"adHighCpu\"' | grep defaultVariant; kubectl -n astronomy-shop logs deploy/flagd -c flagd --tail=3 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; POD=$(kubectl -n astronomy-shop get pods -l opentelemetry.io/name=flagd -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}'); kubectl -n astronomy-shop logs $POD -c init-config 2>&1 | grep -A8 '\"adHighCpu\"' | grep defaultVariant"
    ],
    "exit_code": 0,
    "image": "sremut-agent:k8s-1.32",
    "is_error": false,
    "limit_reached": false,
    "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
    "seconds": 99,
    "summary": "The root cause was the `adHighCpu` feature flag defaulting to `on`, which makes the ad service burn CPU on every request. I set it to `off` and restarted the affected services. All pods are Running and Ready, and the ad service's CPU use dropped from about 1171m to about 8m.\n\n**What I found**\n- Every pod was Ready with zero restarts, but `ad` was using about 1.17 cores with no CPU limit set, so it was starving the node.\n- In the `flagd-config` ConfigMap, `adHighCpu` had `defaultVariant: \"on\"`. It is the only fault-injection flag defaulted on. The other flags, including `adManualGc` and `adFailure`, were off.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Set `adHighCpu.defaultVariant` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap, using `kubectl apply` on the ConfigMap.\n- Restarted `flagd` so its init container re-copied the corrected file. The init container's output confirms the new pod is serving `\"off\"`.\n- Restarted `ad` to pick up the flag change.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The ConfigMap is managed by the Helm release `astronomy-shop`. A `helm upgrade` will restore the chart's values, so the fix should also go into the Helm values if this is meant to persist.\n- The `kubectl apply` warning about the missing last-applied annotation is harmless; kubectl added it.",
    "timed_out": false,
    "turns": 12,
